{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527982-cheat-the-scale-of-anubis","id":1527982,"title":"Cheat the Scale of Anubis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-04T23:01:38-08:00","id":1527982,"title":"Cheat the Scale of Anubis","content":"After the discussion in the <b>Ministry's </b>discipline Tstart to wonder what's the deal with the ultimate goal of the Cheat the Scale of Anubis power<br /> <br /> \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 <b>Cheat the Scale of Anubis</b> (DA Rev)<br /> This serves the same as the modern level Heart of Darkness allowing the Setite to remove his heart or enshroud himself in a cocoon that is virtually impossible to harm. This power can only be performed in the dark of the night--either after the moon has set, before it has risen or during the new moon--and only on oneself. Once the Setite has removed his heart and other vital organs, he must place them in specially prepared urns (called canopic jars). After the vampire has removed all his major organs, his vitae and undead flesh combine to wrap him in a dry, scaly shroud that is nearly impenetrable. Only a small opening over his mouth remains in the shroud. The character then falls into a sort of torpor. Only feeding him his removed internal organs will awaken him. Once that is complete, it takes about a minute for the cocoon to crumble to dust. The enshrouded vampire is virtually impossible to harm--no known direct force, from inferno to sunlight, can do him damage. However, the extracted organs are vunerable, most especially the heart. Exposing it to fire or sunlight causes the vampire's instant death. Although terrible, this destruction is actually final part of the ritual--in which the vampire's followers burn his organs before a statue of Set. By meeting his Final Death in this way, the Setite reaches Anubis without a heart and is hence able to pass by without ever undertaking the test of the scales, entering the afterlife as a powerful agent of his god.<br /> It is possible to undertake this ritual part way, something usually done for two reasons. The first is to assume the fully enshrouded form for protection's aske, which some Setites do when they are traveling. Their ghouls carry them as cargo in a ship or caravan and then their master his organs when they arrive at their destination. The enshrouded form is completely immune to harm. No source of injury--save perhaps the might of a Methuselah or Antediluvian--can do it direct physical damage. The other option is to stop the ritual with the removal of the heart. This makes him immune to standard or diablerie. However, if an enemy gets hold of the Canopic jar containing the extracted organ, the vampire is in seriously trouble. Any vampire who witnesses the process is subject to Rotchreck. The removed organs are rich with vitae. Most contain one blood point's worth (which reduces the vampire's overall blood pool), and that blood remains fresh in the withered organ-meat. A ghoul or vampire who consumes a Setite's removed organ takes one step toward the Blood Oath as normal. The heart contains two blood points and a vampire consuming it is attempting diablerie against the Setite. Once the two blood points are drained, the attacker passes straight to the heart's blood. Staking the heart, puts the Setite in torpor.<br /> <br /> Now, the whole point of this ritual is this part<br /> <b>&quot;By meeting his Final Death in this way, the Setite reaches Anubis without a heart and is hence able to pass by without ever undertaking the test of the scales, <u>entering the afterlife as a powerful agent of his god.</u>&quot;</b><br /> <br /> But... what that actually means?<br /> Have you ever used it? How would you use it if a player would wants to actually complete the Ritual?<br /> Whats your two deben in this matter?<br /> <br /> The Follower of Set becomes a Wraith?<br /> Demon of Duat or a Bane of sort that is a prime material for creating &quot;lesser&quot; Bane mummies, an <b>Asekh-Sen</b> or a Hybrid Mummy made by the Akhu Ritual of the same name?<br /> It become something that is actually capable to harass the Dark Kingdom of Sand and the Mummies while they dead?<br /> <br /> I'm curious about your ideas!<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T02:21:10-08:00","id":1528092,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is that Followers of Set are hinted to have a fantastic connection to Duat, so strong and deep that even some Cappadocians went to them to learn (Lazarus and co., which is framed as &quot;Caps learn from Setites&quot; in VDA20 Tome of Secrets), but this has hardly ever been detailed. Set himself is believed by some to be in Duat, and so are the Setites old enemies like Osiris, Anubis and the mummies when they are not active in the living world. If all this had been given some concrete effect on the game, such as Setites having their own Necromancy and means of travelling the Underworld, it would make sense, but unfortunately it's all left very undefined. <br /> Cheat the Scale of Anubis could be a great tool to justify transforming elder Setites into some Duat-dwelling being with Duat-related superpowers to both serve Set's agenda over there and influencing the clan indirectly in the living world. They could become some type of counter-mummies who cannot return physically to the living world but have massive mystic manipulation powers to still exert their will on it through cults and servants.<br /> One then has to decide whether they actually find Set on the other side and what his goal is. There's all sorts of options with that in the lore: he could be a saint under coverage, truly trying to save the world, for example, but has to keep a bad rep and spread corruption to succeed in his mission, like it's hinted at in VDA20 Companion or sort of suggested in Libellus Sanguinis. Mind you, the Shadowlands, using crossover material from previous editions and Demon the Fallen (but i havent read the manuals on this, only the wikis online), are supposed to be a demon-created realm for humans to avoid going wherever it is that they would be going after death because demons had no clue about that and only saw human death as a sad and cruel decision of God. It's therefore not too difficult to frame Osiris as a bad guy who is trapping human souls in an unnecessary afterlife built on top of Oblivion/Apep's realm, and from that position he has been able to manipulate human beliefs in a way that restricts them unnecessarily while also benefitting Osiris. Set somehow figured out the mess and is out there trying to destroy this delusion and let human souls actually move on to their rightful destination and stop being afraid of destruction and Apep. This is just one option from a Setite fan. There are obviously many others, up to each ST.<br /> <br /> Unless one writes mechanics for what happens when using this power FOR Final Death, this just seems like a flavour tool for Setites as antagonists. The idea itself of removing your heart and hiding it or entering an indestructible torpor while relying on your loyal servants to wake you up is very bad for PCs, only good for NPCs, and I'm glad this has been turned into a 5th level ritual of Setite Sorcery in VDA20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}